+# E29). The 1.2 fixture is residential(0) <- router(1) -> content_host(2),
+# 12 tiles apart on row y=15. Draw source->router, then TWO router->sink pipes
+# (a 2-member bundle, pooled cap 30 = the packet bandwidth -> 1-tick transit).
+# Spawn one packet residential(0) -> content_host(2) at 1000ms (tick 20).
+#
+# The packet reaches the router (tick 22) + forwards onto the bundle's
+# representative pipe (pipe 1) at tick 23. At 1150ms (tick 24) the representative
+# is DEMOLISHED mid-traversal: the packet drops back to the router, the bundle
+# rebuilds to one survivor (cap shrinks 30 -> 15), and the packet RE-FORWARDS via
+# the survivor (E29 — no stale route) + still delivers (tick 27). Graceful
+# shrink, not a hard cut; traffic continues. Only full-bundle-loss would drop
+# the route (E1).
+#
+# T2 pixel captures are deferred (the rlsw-harness gap); this golden pins the
+# post-demolish state via T1 hashes + the replay gate (the demolish is a logged
+# command, re-applied identically on every replay — ODN-11).
+seed 42
+run 4000ms
+at 500ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 500ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 500ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 1000ms spawn 0 2
+at 1150ms demolish pipe 1
+expect hash stable
